  "answer": "Windows Terminal already supports this. Open settings.json (Settings > Open JSON file) and set the profile's colorScheme to a light/dark pair, for example: \"colorScheme\": {\"light\": \"One Half Light\", \"dark\": \"One Half Dark\"}. Terminal will then switch the color scheme automatically with the app theme (set the app theme to 'Use Windows theme'). You can also set this under profiles.defaults to apply to all profiles. It currently has to be edited in JSON because it's not yet in the settings UI (tracked in #16984). See the docs page on profile appearance > color scheme."
